  S-terms with opaque variables (atoms); the head machine [a, b, c] ++ R => args a ++ [c, b·c] ++ R needs an S-headed
  front, so an atom-headed front is stuck (the run "opens a variable"). M35 is given as a base-35 bignum table; its
  S-identity, closure and head-normal-form facts and the witness tables are checked by the kernel (`decide +kernel`).
  An assignment rho sends atoms to M35 classes; `clsv rho` is the polynomial of a term on M35.
  * `thH_b` (H(b)): every symbolic run preserves the polynomial on M35, for every assignment.
  * `thH_a` (H(a)): if the symbolic run reaches a head normal form (a list of length <= 2), the polynomial lies in F
    for every assignment.
  * `corH1` (no clean holding): for all closed g1, g2 the run of S g1 g2 x w never reaches a head normal form — it opens
    x or w, or diverges.
  * `corH2` (holding two data): for every closed K whose M35 class is not in Safe2 = [0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16] (the six nest classes
    S, SS, S(SS), S(S(SS)), S(S(S(SS))), S(S(S(S(SS))))), the run of K x y never reaches a head normal form.
  * `corH3` (no S-term holds three data): for every closed K the run of K x y z never reaches a head normal form.
